---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import source from '../../../lib/paperwork/source.json';
---
<Base title="Configure Paperwork" description="Prepare an independently owned browser-local PDF editor with a reviewed source pin and portable configuration.">
<a href="/init">← Init</a><h1>Your own Paperwork.</h1><p class="lede">Set the editor’s title, introduction and starting theme. Download the configuration, then reproduce the independently maintained app from its reviewed source.</p>
<p><a href={source.origin}>Open Paperwork</a> · <a href="/paperwork">See the working editor</a></p>
<form id="paperwork-config"><label>Title<input name="title" value="Paperwork" required maxlength="80"/></label><label>Introduction<textarea name="intro" maxlength="240">Fill the fields. Write on the page. Add your signature.</textarea></label><label>Starting theme<select name="theme"><option value="midnight">Dark</option><option value="daylight">Light</option></select></label><div class="actions"><button type="submit">Download configuration</button><button type="button" class="secondary" id="paperwork-copy">Copy creation request</button></div><p id="paperwork-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p></form>
<section class="section"><h2>Reproduce the app.</h2><p>Give the configuration to your agent in an authorised workspace. The existing Init command copies the exact reviewed source into a new directory and applies these three settings. It preserves existing projects and performs no install or deployment.</p><pre><code>{`git clone https://github.com/loftwah/app-composer-paperwork.git
cd app-composer-paperwork
git checkout ${source.commit}
# From the App Composer checkout:
pnpm init:paperwork --source /absolute/app-composer-paperwork \\
  --destination /absolute/new-paperwork --config /absolute/paperwork.json`}</code></pre><p>In the new project: <code>pnpm install --frozen-lockfile</code>, <code>pnpm check</code>, <code>pnpm build</code>, then review its own target and release guard. The generated Cloudflare target is deliberately unconfigured. The reference target belongs to this reference instance; a reproduced project needs its own reviewed target before deployment.</p><p>Configuration contains interface text and theme only. PDFs and signatures never enter Composer, a specification or a database.</p><a href={source.repository+'/tree/'+source.commit}>Inspect the exact source</a></section>
<script src="../../lib/paperwork-client.ts"></script>
</Base>
<style>#paperwork-config{max-width:680px}pre{white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere}label{margin-block:16px}</style>
